  /**
   * Send a Markdown (.md) or HTML (.html) report as a document — like a Claude Artifact. HTML may carry CSS/JS/images alongside it and opens inside the app in a sandboxed, script-limited view; nothing it does can ever reach off the device. Two ways to provide the content: (1) inline — filename + text_content, with assets[] (up to 200 files, each text_content or content_base64) for anything an HTML document links to by relative path; or (2) staged — stage the main file and any assets first with upload_file/create_upload_url, then pass their upload_id as main_upload_id and asset_upload_ids (largest option, up to 2 GB each). asset_paths, parallel to asset_upload_ids, names the relative path each staged asset is linked by; omit it to use each upload's own file name. REQUIRES model_name. Posts one group message carrying the document as an attachment. schedule_at (RFC3339) schedules it instead — inline only, no assets. client_message_id (optional, your own UUID) makes a retried call safe — see send_message.
   *
   * <p>Tool: {@code send_document}.
   *
   * @param conversationId required
   * @param options optional arguments (all nullable), by JSON name:
   *     {@code asset_paths} (List&lt;String&gt;) Optional, parallel to asset_upload_ids: the relative path each staged asset is linked by. Omit an entry (or the whole array) to use that upload's own file name instead.
   *     {@code asset_upload_ids} (List&lt;String&gt;) Staged assets, by upload_id. Combined with assets, at most 200 total.
   *     {@code assets} (List&lt;Object&gt;) Inline assets. Combined with asset_upload_ids, at most 200 total.
   *     {@code caption} (String) 
   *     {@code client_message_id} (String) Optional. Your own UUID for this send, at most 64 characters. A second call naming the same id returns the message the first call already sent instead of posting a duplicate document.
   *     {@code filename} (String) Inline path only. Must end .md, .markdown, .html or .htm.
   *     {@code main_upload_id} (String) Staged path only, instead of filename+text_content: an upload_id from upload_file/create_upload_url. Its staged file name must end .md, .markdown, .html or .htm.
   *     {@code model_name} (String) 
   *     {@code reply_to_id} (String) 
   *     {@code schedule_at} (String) RFC3339. Schedules instead of sending now — inline document only (filename + text_content), no assets, no main_upload_id. Result carries scheduled_message_id and send_at.
   *     {@code silent} (boolean) Send with no sound — the push still arrives, but silently.
   *     {@code text_content} (String) Inline path only. The document's own content, UTF-8 text.
   *     {@code topic_id} (String) Optional: "general" or an id from list_topics. A reply goes into the topic of the message it answers.
   * @return the tool result; throws {@link McpException.Tool} when the tool answers isError
   */
